  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammed Gaus Ismail Mohammed vs The State Of Maharashtra on 20 October, 2022 Author: N.R. Borkar Bench: N.R. Borkar Digitally signed by Prajakta Prajakta Sagar Sagar Vartak Vartak Date: 2022.10.21 15:56:05 +0530 Prajakta Vartak 8-Aba 2964-22.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2964 Of 2022 Mohammed Gaus Ismail Mohammed ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ......... Mr. Veerdhaval Kakade for the Applicant. Mr. A. R. Kapadnis, App for the State. ......... Coram : N.R. Borkar, J. Dated : 20th October, 2022. P.C. :- 1. This is an application filed under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for grant of anticipatory bail. 2 . The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No.368 of 2022 registered at Solapur Police Station, Solapur Rural for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3) (e), 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "This is an application filed under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for grant of anticipatory bail. The learned APP seeks time to verify criminal antecedents of the present applicant.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is the owner of the truck and he has nothing to do with the seized tobacco products as the truck was given on hire to transporter. He further submits that nothing is to be recovered at the instance of the applicant and hence there is no need of custodial interrogation of the applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is the owner of the truck and he has nothing to do with the seized tobacco products as the truck was given on hire to transporter. He further submits that nothing is to be recovered at the instance of the applicant and hence there is no need of custodial interrogation of the applicant.",
